WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
The Qur'an points to the sky, the
rain and the turning of night and day,

2
00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.680
and calls them signs.

3
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.450
It says the heavens and
earth were once joined,

4
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.790
then split apart, and every
living thing was made from water.

5
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.110
Then Allah tells the angels
he will place a khalifah,

6
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.000
a steward, on earth.

7
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:24.120
The angels ask: will you place there one
who will cause mischief and shed blood?

8
00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.460
So why would Allah trust
humans with the earth?

9
00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:32.450
In this mission, you'll explore how the
Qur'an describes the making of the universe.

10
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.360
Then you'll follow the story
of Adam and the angels,

11
00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.220
and see what being a steward means today.

12
00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: discover how the
Qur'an answers the angels' question.
